cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the Ion Optics Workbench, please cite it as below, with the
  version you used. The ion masses of the nuclide builder are from the AME2020
  atomic mass evaluation; cite those papers too when the masses matter.
title: Ion Optics Workbench
abstract: >-
  A browser tool for electrostatic and magnetic charged-particle optics: it
  solves Laplace's or Poisson's equation on a two-dimensional planar or
  cylindrically symmetric grid with exact sub-grid electrode boundaries, and
  traces ions and electrons relativistically through lenses, mirrors, energy
  analyzers, time-of-flight spectrometers, RF devices and magnetic fields,
  with lens, time-of-flight, emittance and capacitance analysis and a
  validation suite against published and exact values.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Foley
    given-names: Casey D.
    website: "https://cdfoley.com"
version: "0.2.4"
date-released: "2026-11-11"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/foley-photon/ion-optics-workbench"
url: "https://cdfoley.com/beta/ion-optics/"
keywords:
  - ion optics
  - charged-particle optics
  - electrostatic lens
  - einzel lens
  - time of flight
  - trajectory simulation
  - finite differences
  - multigrid
